Files
-----
Clinic.java  -- the harness (port of clinic.py), plus Toolsets.BAD/GOOD
                (port of toolsets.py)
Mine.java    -- your toolset to rewrite (port of mine.py), a separate
                top-level class in the same default package as Clinic

Build & run
------------
javac Clinic.java Mine.java
java Clinic --tools bad
java Clinic --tools good
java Clinic --tools bad mine
java Clinic --tools bad good mine

Requirements at runtime (same as the Python original):
  - a .env file in the working directory with GATEWAY_API_KEY (and optionally
    MODEL, BUDGET_USD, GATEWAY_URL)
  - goals.json in the working directory (or pass --goals path/to/goals.json)
  - python3 on PATH, plus the aira-ops repo checkout, so ThrowawayOps can
    launch day3-integration-security/aira-ops/aira_ops.py the same way
    clinic.py did

Not yet done:
  - Mine.java's TOOLS/run are still the "start from BAD" starting point,
    same as mine.py before you rewrite it. Follow the checklist in the
    file's header comment.

Note: this was authored without a working javac in the conversion sandbox
(the environment's package mirror couldn't install a JDK), so it has been
reviewed by hand rather than compiled. Run `javac Clinic.java Mine.java`
yourself as a first check before relying on it.